WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.760
The ending of Disney's "Haunted Mansion" features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:07.140
a lot of ghouls and too many dancing&nbsp;
ghosts. But it also has fans wondering:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.768
Is a potential sequel in the works? If the ending&nbsp;
is any clue, we may already have our answer.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.440
Before we jump into the film's ending, let's do&nbsp;
a little recap of everything that leads to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.040
big finale. Once single mother Gabbie&nbsp;
and her son Travis enter the mansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.880
they become haunted by various&nbsp;
ghosts. So they call on some experts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.154
including a psychic named Harriet and&nbsp;
a paranormal photographer named Ben.

00:00:28.154 --> 00:00:30.120
"I'm not afraid of a couple ghosts."

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.180
Together, the group tries to uncover&nbsp;
the truth behind the mansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.841
and a particularly treacherous&nbsp;
being known as the Hatbox Ghost.

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:41.460
They eventually discover that the Hatbox Ghost&nbsp;
is formerly Alistair Crump — a socialite who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.080
secretly murdered many people until he was&nbsp;
beheaded by his detractors. As the Hatbox Ghost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:51.420
Alistair has been collecting souls in the mansion&nbsp;
for decades. He hopes to reach 1,000 souls so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.740
he can come back to the world of living. Once the&nbsp;
group learns that Alistair is only one soul away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.120
and is targeting both Ben and Travis due&nbsp;
to their lingering grief, they're forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:04.320
to find something that belonged to him. Once the&nbsp;
group has the belonging, Harriet can perform a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.420
banishing spell with Madame Leota. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
Alistair's got plenty of tricks up his sleeve.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.720
"You're going to be here for quite awhile."

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.980
Alistair can't use any old soul to complete&nbsp;
his plan — it needs to come from a willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.660
volunteer. This is why he targets Ben and Travis.&nbsp;
They're both still dealing with their unresolved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:26.160
feelings over the deaths of loved ones, so they're&nbsp;
vulnerable to Alistair's tricks. Travis nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.260
does when Alistair mimics his father's voice, but&nbsp;
Ben intervenes and stops it. However, this doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.940
stop Alistair from attempting to coax Ben. As a&nbsp;
result, Ben is forced to make a crucial choice:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:41.115
either sacrifice himself to save everyone else&nbsp;
or let Alistair's reign of terror continue.

00:01:41.115 --> 00:01:46.440
From there, Alistair transports Ben, Travis, and&nbsp;
Gabbie to a graveyard. In the graveyard, Alistair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.700
reminds Ben that he'll never be over Alyssa's&nbsp;
death and that giving up his soul will be the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.800
way to see her again. However, Ben doesn't succumb&nbsp;
to Alistair's tricks, and with the help of his new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.325
friends, he defeats Alistair by kicking him into&nbsp;
the open grave below. With a new perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.325 --> 00:02:04.825
Ben has finally come to terms with Alyssa's&nbsp;
death and is able to move forward in life.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.600
Once Alistair is defeated, Ben and Travis&nbsp;
help fulfill the Sea Captain Ghost's final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.560
wish to be brought back to the sea. After&nbsp;
that, Ben gives away Alyssa's belongings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.100
and prepares to start a new chapter in&nbsp;
his life. However, before he leaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.940
he spots a cat sitting on the porch with&nbsp;
the name Tater-Tot on its collar. The name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.980
is tied to a story Ben told about Alyssa's love&nbsp;
of unhealthy food. So it's a reminder of Alyssa.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.400
When the film ends, everyone reunites&nbsp;
at the mansion for a Halloween party,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.711
and even the spirits get down&nbsp;
on some singing and dancing.

00:02:33.238 --> 00:02:37.620
The running themes in "Haunted Mansion" are about&nbsp;
grief and how people live on in memory. Ben,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.180
in particular, is plagued by grief over Alyssa's&nbsp;
death, which affects him throughout the film. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.500
a deeply heartfelt and emotional scene, Ben&nbsp;
talks to the group about how Alyssa's death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.760
still haunts him. He even nearly breaks down in&nbsp;
tears while talking about not knowing whether or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.861
not Alyssa knew he loved her. That uncertainty is&nbsp;
the core reason behind his continual suffering.

00:02:55.861 --> 00:02:59.520
Meanwhile, Harriet is reminded of a lost&nbsp;
loved one by the sounds of train whistles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.600
seeing as they both loved model trains. She&nbsp;
tells Ben that he too will find something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.767
fondly remember Alyssa by, which will help him&nbsp;
move on. For Ben, this is the cat, Tater-Tot.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:12.480
Ben's arc in "Haunted Mansion" is meant to&nbsp;
remind viewers that even when someone is gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.680
their memory still lives on in other ways.&nbsp;
So the biggest takeaway from the ending of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.654
the film is that people can overcome grief&nbsp;
without forgetting the person they've lost.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.320
Once Alistair is pulled back into the ground,&nbsp;
most viewers probably assumed that the rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.160
the spirits would simply disappear and move&nbsp;
on. After all, Alistair was the main thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.240
keeping them in the mansion. However, instead&nbsp;
of vanishing, the ghosts move back into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.860
mansion and begin celebrating Alistair's demise.&nbsp;
Alistair might have been the reason why the ghosts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.520
were haunting everyone in the mansion, but he's&nbsp;
not to blame for why they haven't been able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.200
move on. Like the Sea Captain Ghost, every spirit&nbsp;
that remains in the mansion still has something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.317
they're holding onto in the real world, which is&nbsp;
preventing them from going into the afterlife.

00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:54.180
As Harriet explains, every soul will be&nbsp;
caught in a sort of limbo ghost world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.840
if they leave the world of the living&nbsp;
with regrets or unresolved baggage. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.800
while they would understandably want to party&nbsp;
in the mansion after Alistair is dealt with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.880
there's still some unresolved aspects in their&nbsp;
stories. This is why they can't leave yet.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.900
"These ghosts…"

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.840
"...they're running from something."

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.020
Despite the fact that Disney is always trying&nbsp;
to turn their new films into franchises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.934
"Haunted Mansion" features an ending that&nbsp;
pretty much closes the book on the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:21.120
The end of the film doesn't tease any potential&nbsp;
for Ben and the others to return, nor a way for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.080
the ghosts of the mansion to have their stories&nbsp;
fleshed out. So, it seems like "Haunted Mansion"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.220
could be a one-and-done story for Disney,&nbsp;
which is a rarity in Hollywood nowadays.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.940
However, there are still some avenues&nbsp;
for a potential sequel. A sequel could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.580
easily see Ben and the group deal&nbsp;
with a different haunted mansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.960
or even become acquainted with some of the ghosts&nbsp;
still lurking around the original mansion. Given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.800
the mansion's murder-filled history, there&nbsp;
could even be a new antagonist that rises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.820
up. That antagonist may even be able to&nbsp;
acquire the power that eluded Alistair.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.260
Obviously, a strong box office performance&nbsp;
and positive critical reception could entice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.980
Disney to do more movies in this&nbsp;
world. However, with Disney CEO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.420
Bob Iger's recent comments about downsizing&nbsp;
some of the company's established franchises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:04.921
it's probably more likely that this will be the&nbsp;
only "Haunted Mansion" movie for quite a while.

00:05:04.921 --> 00:05:07.358
"Is this the man who mugged you?"

00:05:07.358 --> 00:05:10.320
"Wow! You just did that just now?"

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.040
Although there hasn't been an announcement&nbsp;
of a sequel to "Haunted Mansion," director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.857
Justin Simien has stated that the door&nbsp;
is open for more stories in this world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.857 --> 00:05:21.300
While talking with SFX Magazine,&nbsp;
Simien mentioned that he believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.358
the film's world-building creates tons of&nbsp;
potential for a sequel. He told the outlet:

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:27.374
"It's definitely in the realm of possibility."

00:05:27.374 --> 00:05:30.660
Simien also said that a lot of thought&nbsp;
went into fleshing out the world that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.260
the movie takes place in, before adding,
"It was really just about expanding what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.521
we know and what we can see around the story just&nbsp;
a bit further, but not filling in every blank."

00:05:38.521 --> 00:05:39.492
He then went on to say:

00:05:39.492 --> 00:05:42.900
"We certainly set up a lot that I think&nbsp;
a lot of other stories could derive from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.479
and continue from. Not really up to me, but I&nbsp;
definitely think there are possibilities there."&nbsp;

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:50.700
Simien went even further in talking&nbsp;
about how the film's depiction of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:55.057
Hatbox Ghost can be applied to other&nbsp;
ghouls within the story. He told SFX,

00:05:55.057 --> 00:05:56.689
"We're pulling from what has been established,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.240
what really has been rumored, and tried&nbsp;
to flesh him out and flesh that story out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.375
too. I think it's really satisfying. But it&nbsp;
also leaves the door open for a lot more."

00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:06.360
While the decision lies with the higher-ups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.442
the director clearly sees potential for&nbsp;
"Haunted Mansion" to be further explored.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.571
Even if a direct sequel doesn't&nbsp;
happen, there are other ways that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.571 --> 00:06:17.460
Disney could continue the story of these&nbsp;
characters and this world. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.820
there could be spin-off films focusing&nbsp;
on the stories of the various ghosts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.240
kind of like what The Conjuring Universe&nbsp;
does with its spooky characters. Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.080
could even make a villain-focused origin&nbsp;
movie for the Hatbox Ghost, just like they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.991
did with "Maleficent" and "Cruella". And if&nbsp;
they wanted an alternative to the big screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:36.565
in order to keep costs down, Disney+ would be&nbsp;
a great place for "Haunted Mansion" content.

00:06:36.565 --> 00:06:40.500
Moreover, an animated series focusing on&nbsp;
the film's characters and ghosts could be an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.367
absolute blast and deliver some family-friendly&nbsp;
horror that audiences of all ages would enjoy.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:49.080
Another "Haunted Mansion" crossover could&nbsp;
also be worth looking into. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:53.040
it already happened not too long ago with "Muppets&nbsp;
Haunted Mansion," which most critics loved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:57.000
Imagine how fun it would be to see Mickey Mouse&nbsp;
or other Disney characters going through their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.200
own terrifying journey in the "Haunted Mansion"&nbsp;
franchise. Frankly, it sounds like a perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.940
recurring Halloween special for the streamer.&nbsp;
Another great idea is an anthology series based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.094
on the ghosts of the mansion, with a new ghoul's&nbsp;
past fleshed out every week in a new episode.

00:07:10.094 --> 00:07:12.960
"Death lurks around every corner."

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.980
"Haunted Mansion" is far from being the first&nbsp;
of Disney's theme park rides to get its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:21.992
movie — and it definitely won't be the last.&nbsp;
Along with a sequel to 2021's "Jungle Cruise,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.992 --> 00:07:26.160
Disney is set to develop more "Pirates of the&nbsp;
Caribbean" movies, as well as movies based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.660
rides like "Big Thunder Mountain Railroad" and&nbsp;
"Space Mountain." While it's clear that Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.200
isn't pumping the brakes on trying to bring&nbsp;
their most famous rides onto the big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.400
the lack of franchise building in the ending&nbsp;
of "Haunted Mansion" could be a sign that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.820
the company's other ride-inspired&nbsp;
movies might also just be one-offs.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.540
Aside from "Pirates of the Caribbean,"&nbsp;
none of Disney's ride adaptations have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.080
been successful enough or garnered a&nbsp;
big enough fanbase to keep them afloat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:52.980
for multiple pictures. If "Haunted Mansion"&nbsp;
does well, maybe that would change. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.700
the ending of "Haunted Mansion" makes it&nbsp;
pretty obvious that Disney doesn't intend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.660
on churning out multiple movies unless they&nbsp;
determine there's an appetite for them. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.920
the upcoming "Big Thunder Mountain Railroad" and&nbsp;
"Space Mountain" films — as well as any other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:09.782
ride adaptations Disney decides to make in the&nbsp;
future — will likely be standalone adventures.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.000
As mentioned earlier, the idea of other franchises&nbsp;
crossing over with "The Haunted Mansion" isn't all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.140
that strange since it happened not too long ago.&nbsp;
From Mickey and his friends having an animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.680
horror adventure to Marvel characters&nbsp;
taking a trip to the iconic horror site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.520
there are plenty of cool crossovers that&nbsp;
would be incredible to see. But you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:31.352
what would be a really amazing crossover? One&nbsp;
with Disney's' 2003 "Haunted Mansion" movie.

00:08:31.352 --> 00:08:34.477
While it would be tough to believe that&nbsp;
these movies take place in the same world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.477 --> 00:08:37.920
there's surely a storyline that could&nbsp;
bring these two universes together. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.280
idea of seeing LaKeith Stanfield,&nbsp;
who plays Ben in the 2023 film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.894
and Eddie Murphy on the big screen&nbsp;
together sounds like an absolute treat.&nbsp;

00:08:46.205 --> 00:08:48.331
"Dark spirits? Don't you make&nbsp;
no dark spirits come out."

00:08:48.331 --> 00:08:51.480
Sure, it's a wildly ambitious task,&nbsp;
but it's something that Disney could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.840
certainly make happen. And it's just&nbsp;
one of the many potential crossovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:58.461
that could make the "Haunted Mansion"&nbsp;
franchise something truly special.

